      "The crop side works on a simple geometric idea. Most watermarks live at the edges — a corner logo, a platform stamp along the bottom. By scaling the frame up modestly and shifting the visible window, those edge zones fall outside the final picture. Because the zoom is slight, the quality cost is small, though it is real: you are enlarging pixels, so extreme zooms will soften the image.",
      "The text side is template-based, and it is worth being clear about what that means. The tool has patterns for how strong titles and hooks are structured — a curiosity gap, a specific number, a named mistake, a direct promise — and slots your topic into them. Hashtag sets are assembled by mixing broad reach tags with narrower topic tags, which mirrors how experienced creators build theirs.",
      "No part of this reads the platform's algorithm, predicts performance, or copies a specific viral video. It systematizes the part of packaging that is genuinely repeatable, and leaves the judgment — what is true, funny, or interesting about your clip — to you.",
      "Step by step",
      "Start with the video itself. If a watermark needs to leave the frame, load the clip, apply the gentlest zoom that clears the edge, and watch the result through once. Check that faces, captions burned into the footage, and anything near the edges you actually need are still comfortably in frame before exporting.",
      "Next, generate the packaging. Enter your topic plainly — 'beginner home workout, no equipment' beats 'fitness video' — because the templates can only be as specific as what you feed them. Generate a batch of titles, hooks and captions, and read them as raw material.",
      "Then edit like a creator, not a customer. Pick the title that makes the most honest promise your video keeps. Take the hook and say it out loud; if it sounds like an advert, rewrite it the way you would actually talk. Trim the caption to what adds context or personality, and choose hashtags that genuinely match the content over ones that merely look popular.",
      "Post, then pay attention to what your own analytics tell you over several videos. Patterns in your niche beat any generic template, and within a few weeks you will be using the generator mostly for warm-up ideas on days when your brain is empty.",
      "Who it helps most",
      "New creators benefit most, because packaging is the skill they have had least time to practice. Having ten structured title options beats staring at an empty title box, and learning why the options work teaches the craft faster than posting into the void.",
      "Small businesses making their own short videos — the café filming its morning bake, the salon showing a transformation — get the same lift: a repeatable routine that turns 'we should post something' into a finished, presentable clip without hiring an agency. Social media freelancers managing several accounts use the kit as a first-draft machine, then spend their billed time on the editing and judgment clients actually pay for.",
      "Honest limits",
      "Templates cannot make a dull video interesting, and no title rescues content that does not hold attention past the first seconds. The tool also cannot tell you what will trend next week; anyone who claims otherwise is selling something. Treat every generated line as a draft that needs your voice, your facts and your humour.",
      "The watermark crop has hard edges too — literally. It only handles marks at the frame's edge; a watermark in the centre of the picture cannot be zoomed away, and heavy cropping of a low-resolution clip will visibly soften it. And a necessary word on rights: removing marks does not create permission. Only rework footage you own or are licensed to use.",
      "Finally, platform rules and trends move. Hashtag habits and caption styles that work now will drift; your own results remain the only reliable guide.",
      "The bottom line",
      "Short-form packaging is a craft of small, repeatable decisions. A tool that cleans the frame and drafts the words from solid templates gives you a running start — the taste, honesty and consistency that actually build an audience stay, as they should, with you.",
      "FAQ",
      "Will these titles and hashtags make my video go viral? There is no honest way to promise that. The tool gives you well-structured drafts based on patterns that commonly work; your content and consistency do the rest.",
      "Can it remove a watermark from the middle of a video? No. The zoom-and-crop approach only pushes marks at the edges out of frame, and it works best on clips you own or have permission to edit.",
      "Do I need to post the generated caption word for word? Please do not. Rewrite it in your own voice — viewers can smell a template, and your personality is the asset the tool cannot generate."
